(7302014, 1138367, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Parabelle:</b></div><hr/><i> Fantastic shot, Anita! Curious if the blurry water was achieved solely by the 1/6s shutter speed, or also changed some in post. <br/> <br/>Exceptionally painterly and quite lovely! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks....it was mainly due to the slow shutter...I added a touch of glam glow, reduced noise and darkened and lightened center, and reduced opacity on select parts...not a lot of editing.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-01-15 02:46:01.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Parabelle: Fantastic shot, Anita! Curious if the blurry water was achieved solely by the 1/6s shutter speed, or also changed some in post.  Exceptionally painterly and quite lovely!   Thanks....it was mainly due to the slow shutter...I added a touch of glam glow, reduced noise and darkened and lightened center, and reduced opacity on select parts...not a lot of editing.', '2015-01-14 09:03:14.000000', '2015-01-15 02:46:01.000000', 0),
